{"pr": 39021, "type": "features", "branch": "9.0.x", "title": "Bring back the ability to fill the login fields from the URL query params", "url": "https://github.com/PrestaShop/PrestaShop/pull/39021", "issue": 38981, "issue_title": "Fields of login page can't be pre-filled on PS v9", "issue_body": "### Prerequisites\n\n- [x] I understand and accept the project's [code of conduct](https://github.com/PrestaShop/PrestaShop/blob/develop/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md).\n- [x] I have already [searched in existing issues](https://github.com/PrestaShop/PrestaShop/issues?q=is%3Aissue+label%3ABug) and found no previous report of this bug.\n\n### Describe the bug and add attachments\n\nWhen you add the following parameters on the login page, the fields of the form are automatically filled: `[admin]/index.php?controller=AdminLogin&email=demoen@prestashop.com&password=prestashop_demo`\n\n![Image](https://github.com/user-attachments/assets/a997eaba-2979-4013-9f89-82816cc3e10d)\n\nThis was useful on demonstration websites to ease the connection to the back office.\nBased on the history of the pull request it seems to be more a forgotten feature than a expected removal.\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nThe form is pre-filled when specific parameters are provided.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. Open your back office login page: The form must be empty, or eventually with the last login used\n2. Add the following parameters: `email=demo@prestashop.com&password=prestashop_demo` and load the page: The form should appear with the details in the fields, ready for submission.\n\nThis process works on PS 8 and below, but not anymore on PS 9\n\n### PrestaShop version(s) where the bug happened\n\n9.0.0\n\n### PHP version(s) where the bug happened\n\n8.1.19\n\n### If your bug is related to a module, specify its name and its version\n\n_No response_\n\n### Your company or customer's name goes here (if applicable).\n\n@PrestaShopCorp", "base_commit": "4d26515fc77bf8eaf023ee7d433a0a4b3f4d2b89", "merge_commit": "e3fd6b90c827b319aa8c35563ea1cdef1bb59dae", "files": ["src/PrestaShopBundle/Form/Admin/Login/LoginType.php"], "lines": 16, "labels": ["QA ✔️", "Feature", "9.0.x"]}
